This repository and the published binaries include or link third-party
software:

libghostty-vt (vendor/libghostty-vt/)
  Prebuilt static archives of libghostty-vt from ghostty-org/ghostty.
  Copyright (c) 2024 Mitchell Hashimoto, Ghostty contributors. MIT License:
  vendor/libghostty-vt/LICENSE. Build provenance:
  vendor/libghostty-vt/PROVENANCE.md. The archives are statically linked into
  the nd-hello (Linux) and nd-shell (macOS) host binaries.

zig-gobject bindings (vendor/gobject-bindings/)
  Machine-generated Zig bindings produced by ianprime0509/zig-gobject at
  commit 97caf8bfb4386409aab1160f7ec05c32ee6d5d7d (pin recorded in
  build.zig.zon and scripts/regen-bindings.sh). Copyright Ian Johnson,
  Zero-Clause BSD (0BSD): vendor/gobject-bindings/LICENSE. The bindings are
  derived from GObject-Introspection GIR data belonging to GTK, GLib, and
  libadwaita.

GTK4, libadwaita, GLib, Pango, Cairo, and related libraries
  The Linux host binary nd-hello (shipped in the @nativedesktop/host-linux-x64
  npm package and as a GitHub Release asset) dynamically links GTK4,
  libadwaita, GLib/GObject/GIO, Pango, Cairo, gdk-pixbuf, and graphene by
  soname. These libraries are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
  License 2.1 or later. No LGPL code is bundled in any published npm tarball
  or release asset; the libraries are loaded from the user's system at run
  time. The LGPL section 6 relink right is satisfied by dynamic linking and by
  the published build instructions in this repository (build from source with
  `zig build`). Optional features additionally dlopen, by bare soname,
  WebKitGTK (<webview>), GStreamer (audio), and libsecret (credentials); each
  feature degrades cleanly when its library is absent. See
  docs/runtime-deps.md for the full runtime contract.

The macOS host binary nd-shell links only Apple system frameworks plus the
statically linked components listed above.
